WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:08.330
Pollyanna was late for supper that night, but it didn't matter.

2
00:00:08.331 --> 00:00:15.166
While Pollyanna was out, Aunt Polly had received a telegram that her cousin had died.

3
00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:20.053
"Your aunt left right away for the funeral in Boston," Nancy explained.

4
00:00:20.054 --> 00:00:24.322
"I guess we can be glad she'll be gone for three days."

5
00:00:24.323 --> 00:00:32.579
"Oh, no, there are some things—like funerals—that you can't play the game with! Now

6
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.108
let me tell you why I'm late." Soon

7
00:00:36.109 --> 00:00:45.977
Nancy was listening in amazement as Pollyanna described Mr. Pendleton's accident and how she'd helped him. ***

8
00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:50.299
The next day Pollyanna met Jimmy by the side of the road.

9
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:58.197
She explained to the disappointed boy that the Ladies' Aiders preferred to help overseas orphans.

10
00:00:58.198 --> 00:01:06.763
He kicked a stone down the road. "Wouldn't it be great if somebody far away wanted me?"

11
00:01:06.764 --> 00:01:09.941
Pollyanna clapped her hands with glee.

12
00:01:09.942 --> 00:01:12.742
"I'll write to my Ladies' Aiders out West.

13
00:01:12.743 --> 00:01:16.763
They're so far away that maybe they'll want you!"

14
00:01:16.764 --> 00:01:22.587
"Don't forget to say that I'll work," Jimmy reminded her.

15
00:01:22.588 --> 00:01:28.984
*** About a week later, Pollyanna went into the sitting room to see Aunt Polly, who was back from Boston.

16
00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:35.051
"Aunt Polly, would you mind if I took Mrs. Snow's beef stew to someone else this week?"

17
00:01:35.052 --> 00:01:41.307
Aunt Polly looked up from her knitting. "What are you up to now, Pollyanna?"

18
00:01:41.308 --> 00:01:44.414
"Nothing you could possibly object to."

19
00:01:44.415 --> 00:01:48.900
Pollyanna came over and sat on the footstool near Aunt Polly's chair.

20
00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:54.058
"You let me take stew to her , so I thought you'd let me take it to

21
00:01:54.059 --> 00:01:58.890
him . You see, his broken leg will be a problem for only a

22
00:01:58.891 --> 00:02:02.845
few weeks. But Mrs. Snow is a

23
00:02:02.846 --> 00:02:07.686
lifelong invalid. There will be plenty of opportunities to take her stew

24
00:02:07.687 --> 00:02:14.316
every week." "Him? His broken leg? What on earth are you

25
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:17.119
talking about?" "It all happened while you were

26
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.782
away." Pollyanna got a faraway look in her eyes as she recalled that

27
00:02:21.783 --> 00:02:27.694
day. "I found him in the woods and had to unlock his house and call the

28
00:02:27.695 --> 00:02:31.368
doctor. Of course, then I came home, and I haven't seen him

29
00:02:31.369 --> 00:02:34.660
since. But Nancy was making beef stew this

30
00:02:34.661 --> 00:02:40.191
morning. And I thought it would be nice to take it to him. May I, Aunt

31
00:02:40.192 --> 00:02:46.425
Polly?" "Yes, I suppose so." Aunt Polly

32
00:02:46.426 --> 00:02:50.970
sighed. She sometimes felt worn down by conversations with

33
00:02:50.971 --> 00:02:53.490
Pollyanna. "Who did you say he

34
00:02:53.491 --> 00:02:56.146
was?" "Mr. John

35
00:02:56.147 --> 00:03:01.504
Pendleton." Aunt Polly sprang from her chair. "John

36
00:03:01.505 --> 00:03:05.990
Pendleton!" "Yes, Nancy told me his name. Maybe you know

37
00:03:05.991 --> 00:03:12.319
him?" Aunt Polly didn't answer but quietly sat down. "Do you know him?"

38
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.898
"Oh, yes. He always smiles and speaks to me now.

39
00:03:16.899 --> 00:03:21.960
He's only grumpy on the outside, you know." Pollyanna stood up.

40
00:03:21.961 --> 00:03:26.036
"I'll go and get the stew from Nancy."

41
00:03:26.037 --> 00:03:31.056
Pollyanna was halfway across the room when Aunt Polly stopped her.

42
00:03:31.057 --> 00:03:37.881
"Wait! I've changed my mind." Aunt Polly's voice was suddenly stern.

43
00:03:37.882 --> 00:03:42.723
"I'd prefer that Mrs. Snow have that stew today as usual."

44
00:03:42.724 --> 00:03:45.851
Pollyanna's disappointment was clear.

45
00:03:45.852 --> 00:03:51.193
"But I want to bring Mr. Pendleton the stew before he gets better.

46
00:03:51.194 --> 00:03:55.250
And he's already had a broken leg for a whole week."

47
00:03:55.251 --> 00:03:58.430
"I do not want to send him stew."

48
00:03:58.431 --> 00:04:03.505
Aunt Polly shook her head to emphasize the "

49
00:04:03.506 --> 00:04:06.634
not ." Pollyanna was not yet ready to give

50
00:04:06.635 --> 00:04:12.237
up. "I understand why you don't like him—he can be awfully grumpy

51
00:04:12.238 --> 00:04:17.827
sometimes. But how about this? I won't tell him that you sent the beef

52
00:04:17.828 --> 00:04:22.077
stew. I'd be glad to say it was from

53
00:04:22.078 --> 00:04:25.684
me." Aunt Polly started to shake her head again but

54
00:04:25.685 --> 00:04:31.749
stopped. She asked in a curiously quiet voice, "Does he know who you

55
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:36.382
are?" Pollyanna sighed. "I don't think

56
00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:41.206
so. I told him my name once, but he never uses

57
00:04:41.207 --> 00:04:46.472
it." "Does he know where you live or that you're my

58
00:04:46.473 --> 00:04:50.084
niece?" "Oh, no. I never told him those

59
00:04:50.085 --> 00:04:55.377
things." For a moment there was silence as Aunt Polly stared blankly into

60
00:04:55.378 --> 00:05:00.656
space. Pollyanna waited impatiently, shifting from one foot to the other.

61
00:05:00.657 --> 00:05:02.778
At last Aunt Polly spoke.

62
00:05:02.779 --> 00:05:08.594
"Very well, you may take the stew to Mr. Pendleton as your own gift.

63
00:05:08.595 --> 00:05:12.735
But let's be perfectly clear about one thing: I didn't send it.

64
00:05:12.736 --> 00:05:15.792
Don't let him think that I did!"

65
00:05:15.793 --> 00:05:18.659
"Yes, ma'am. No, ma'am. Thank you, Aunt Polly!"

66
00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:23.890
Pollyanna exclaimed as she flew from the room.

